    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (currently the `AcceptanceTest` with 2 tests) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint responds via `RespondWithOwner`, which maps the `Owner` entity to `OwnerDto` (generated from `openapi.yml`) through MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`. I implemented the new derived field the same way the existing read-derived fields (`locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`) are done:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so it's generated onto `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping that derives it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n   Returns `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) now pass.",
